00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:13.440
So we've got these.

224
00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:16.000
What about these three techniques that we have?

225
00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:19.000
Simple, consistent formal grammar.

226
00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:22.320
Does natural language give us that?

227
00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:25.560
No. It's complex and inconsistent.

228
00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:28.120
Unambiguous expression of intent.

229
00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:30.160
No, it's ambiguous and vague.

230
00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:33.160
Repeatable. Deterministic.

231
00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:33.960
Not repeatable.

232
00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:36.040
Not deterministic, not version controllable.

233
00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:41.440
As a result, we can if we version control the language that we prompted real with.

234
00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:45.200
That's not enough to get back to the same result again

235
00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:48.760
on its own.

236
00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:50.640
So programing with a

237
00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:54.520
AI presents three important problems

238
00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:57.960
for us to replace traditional programing.

239
00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:03.200
So how do we specify what we want with precision.

240
00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:06.240
That's problem one.

241
00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:11.120
Problem two is how do we confirm that we got what we wanted.

242
00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:14.160
This is the verification problem.

243
00:14:14.440 --> 00:14:17.880
And problem three is that we don't work

244
00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:21.200
in the same way as the machines.

245
00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:26.320
They don't work in the same way as us either way, which you look at that,

246
00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:30.200
the way that we do things is that we tend to deal

247
00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:34.040
with problems with, with the limits of our own context window.

248
00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:36.560
So what will fit inside our heads at a time?

